      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how **Grimoire\u0027s guarded write path journals file state for rollback on failure**.\n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state (either its previous content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- If an agent run fails\u2014whether due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or denied writes\u2014the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed before, or deleting newly created files.\n\n- This mechanism provides **all-or-nothing semantics** for writes without requiring a database transaction. The journal itself acts as the transaction log, maintained only in the process\u0027s memory during a single run.\n\n- The Query agent never uses the rollback functionality since it has no write capability at all.",
